# Core taxonomy and IR

`@rosettadash/core` owns the **component model**, **registry**, **validation**, and **Export IR** — not UI rendering.

## Two graphs (never conflate)

| Graph | Location | Consumers |
|-------|----------|-----------|
| Canvas | `model/types.ts` — `ComponentNode`, bindings, layout | Builder client only |
| Export IR | `ir/types.ts` — `ExportIR`, `IRComponent` | Exporters only |

Pipeline: Canvas → validate → `build-export-ir.ts` → exporters.

**Exporters must never read canvas JSON directly.** If you need a field in export output, add it to IR build — not to exporter hacks.

## Taxonomy permanence

- `ComponentDefinition.type` (dotted key) is **immutable after ship**
- `register()` / `registerPlugin()` **throws** on duplicate type
- Palette: every type in exactly one group; groups hold **2–7 items**

## Manifest sync

Runtime subpaths in `tools/runtime-taxonomy/manifest.mjs` must correspond to registered palette types (or NPM recipe entries). Adding a palette component:

1. `ComponentDefinition` in core registry
2. Manifest entry
3. WC + codegen (see `14-parity-and-codegen.mdc`)

## Shared logic belongs here

| Domain | Module area |
|--------|-------------|
| Equirect filter math | `media/equirect-filter.ts` |
| BYOK / consumer vault | `byok/` |
| Validation rules | `validation/` |
| Presentation sizing | `presentation/` |
| Defaults engine | `defaults/` |

Do not duplicate equirect math or BYOK crypto in runtime packages.

## Label field

- `ComponentNode.label` / `IRComponent.label` — per-instance name; copied by IR build
- `ComponentDefinition.label` — static catalog name ("Bar Chart")
- Renaming instance label is builder UI work — IR already carries it

## Validation before IR

Required relationships (chart needs data source, binding type match, no illegal cycles) belong in `validation/` — not runtime checks inside components.

